  "name": "National Oceanographic Data Centers of Japan, Canada, Russia, and USA",
  "description": "The data base in the Bering Sea includes serial oceanographic stations with observations of parameters such as temperature, salinity, oxygen, pH, alkalinity, phosphates, silicates and nitrates. The total number of stations is about 45,000 from 1932 to 1996.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: The data base was created to carry out the national project \"Russian Seas\".",
